Vcenter root password expired

## Alert

```text
Critical

Alert : Root User Password Expired

Alarm Name : vmware.vcenter.alarm.Rootuserpasswordexpired

Resource : VMware vCenter Server
```

---

## Investigation

Verified the vCenter appliance health.

Confirmed that all vCenter services were running normally.

Connected to the vCenter Server Appliance (VCSA) using the Appliance Management Interface (VAMI) or SSH.

Accessed the vCenter Appliance CLI.

Checked the root account password expiry information.

```bash
chage -l root
```

Verified that the root account password had expired, which triggered the vCenter alarm.

No impact was observed on vCenter services or virtual machine operations.

---

## Root Cause

The root account password on the vCenter Server Appliance had reached its configured password expiration period.

The alarm was generated by the built-in vCenter monitoring system to notify administrators that the appliance root password required renewal.

---

## Resolution

Logged in to the vCenter Appliance CLI using the root account.

Changed the expired root password.

```bash
passwd
```

Verified the updated password expiry information.

```bash
chage -l root
```

After updating the password, the vCenter alarm cleared successfully.

---

## Validation

Verified:

- Root password updated successfully.
- Password expiry information reflected the new expiration date.
- All vCenter services remained healthy.
- No impact to ESXi hosts or virtual machines.
- Root User Password Expired alarm cleared.

